\begin_layout Section
Explainable AI
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
XAI deals with the problem of making AI solutions understandable for humans.
 As described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "XAI_survey"

\end_inset

, a distinction is made between interpretability and explainability.
 Interpretability is defined as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the ability to explain or to present in understandable terms to humans
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and is thus strongly related to the classical version of an explanation
 according to the cambridge dictionary, which defines an explanation as
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the details or reasons that someone gives to make something clear or easy
 to understand
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/explanation
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

 Explanation is, in contrast, rather a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

collection of features of interpretable domain that have contributed for
 a given example to produce a decision
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The best explanation of a simple model is the model itself; it perfectly
 represents itself and is easy to understand.
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "XAI-unified-approach"

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The best explanation is probably the explanation that existed before a model,
 so that the model is a good representation of the explanation.
 
\end_layout

